    trace "Cumulative balance"  x=[2025-01 2025-02]  y=[844.51... 2344.51...]
  => BOTH Living AND Healthcare traces exist AND each carries a February
     point. The February element is the one the fix changes: mutants
     M-hcAmt / M-livingMonth each turn it into `-0` and are killed, which
     is the byte-level proof that the guard sits where the artifact sits.

  /dashboard/charts/data/spending-trend?start=2025-01-01&end=2025-02-28
    {"data":[{"customdata":[[0,520]], ... "x":["2025-02"],"y":[-100]}]}
  => the February customdata entry IS present, and its spend slot is now the
     literal `0` (it was `-0` in my attempt-1 evidence). The test's regexp
     `-0(\.0+)?[,}\]\s]` matches the pre-fix `[[-0,520]]` form (`-0` + `,`)
     and the `y":[220,-0]` form (`-0` + `]`); the live `-100` in y does NOT
     false-positive (it starts `-1`, not `-0`).

Velocity fixture really nets exactly zero (probe on the test's own rows):
  PROBE outflow rows=2 SumAmount=0 rawNeg=-0 signbit=true exactlyZero=true
  PROBE velocity JSON = {"daily_average":0,"historical_daily":0,
                         "month_projection":0,"days_remaining":27,
                         "burn_rate_change":0}
  PROBE DailyAverage sb=false HistoricalDaily sb=false MonthProjection
