FINDINGS (backlog for the lead -- NOT FAIL grounds)
=========================================================================
FINDING 1 (criterion c) -- UNDISCLOSED SURVIVOR, code correct.
`spentSoFar` (insights/trends.go:339) is the SIXTH negated site the brief
listed, and its mutant SURVIVES. The manifest does not disclose this: it
lists only `spend` as an expected survivor and states the velocity test
covers all three velocity sites. The site's code is CORRECT and I PROVE it
is consumer-unobservable at every PRODUCTION surface, so the spec's
disjunctive acceptance line ("load-bearing by mutation OR provably
consumer-unobservable") is satisfied -- but the CB7 precedent is
"acceptable WHEN STATED", and this one is not stated. Proof, so the lead can
write it down:
  1. spentSoFar's ONLY downstream is `monthProjection := spentSoFar +
     (dailyAvg * float64(daysRemaining))`; it is not a field of
     models.SpendingVelocity.
  2. Go probe over the real expression shows the mutant diverges from the
     fix in EXACTLY ONE of nine cases:
        PROJ daysRemaining= 0 dailyAvg= -5.0  mutant=-0 sb=true |
             fixed=0 sb=false  DIVERGES=true
     i.e. only when daysRemaining==0 (today IS the last day of the month;
     daysRemaining = daysInMonth - now.Day()) AND dailyAvg < 0 (a
     refund-dominant selected window) AND the current calendar month's
     outflows net exactly zero. Every other combination is bit-identical.
     Today DaysRemaining=27, so no fixture can reach it -- which is why no
     test can kill this mutant without freezing the clock.
  3. Even in that corner it cannot reach a user: MonthProjection's only
     render path is `{{formatMoney ...}}` at insights.html:207/538/913 and
     insights-verdict-bar.html:35, and formatMoney carries the CB7 -0 belt
     -- PROVEN by mutation: deleting that belt gives
     `render_helpers_test.go:43: formatMoney(-0) = "$-0.00", want "$0.00"`
     (TestFormatMoney fails).
  4. MCP drops it: velocityRowFrom (mcpsvc/spend/trends.go:141-147) copies
     only DailyAverage/HistoricalDaily/BurnRateChange.
  5. The one place raw models.SpendingVelocity is json-encoded
     (handlers/insights/handlers.go:441 in handleVelocityPartial) is the
     `renderer == nil` branch only; cmd/server/main.go:112 always passes a
     non-nil renderer (constructed at main.go:74/78 with an error return),
     so that branch is test-only.
Suggested lead action: record the above in SPEC.md's CB9 note (a doc change,
no code change) so the survivor is "stated" per CB7 precedent.

FINDING 2 (criterion b) -- SAME-CLASS -0 SITES OUTSIDE CB9's SCOPE,
pre-existing, already documented in the code, NOT touched by CB9
(`git diff HEAD` does not list the file):
  internal/services/mcpsvc/spend/summary.go:91  round2(-amt)        byCategoryRows
  internal/services/mcpsvc/spend/summary.go:121 round2(-totals[m])  byMonthRows
  internal/services/mcpsvc/spend/summary.go:144 round2(-total)      byMerchantRows
Consumer: the MCP `summarize_spending` tool's by_category / by_month /
by_merchant rows. The file's own comment at :73-78 already calls this out
("when a category's refunds exactly offset its spend, round2(-amt) can
produce float64 negative zero, which encoding/json renders as the literal
\"-0\" ... Not fixed here"). round2(-0) = math.Round(-0)/100 = -0, so the
token does reach that JSON. A one-line `metrics.SignedNet`-style
normalisation at each of the three sites would close the class repo-wide.
Out of CB9's manifest and pre-existing -> backlog, not a FAIL.

